s) (since next attempt index), memory_append = {\"reflection\": last_attempt[\"reflection\"], \"signature\": last_attempt[\"failure_signature\"]}. But note: The reflection from the last attempt must be nonempty? It is nonempty in fixtures. Should we validate? Probably assume it's nonempty.\n\nEdge: what if attempts length is less than max_attempts but last attempt succeeded? Then stop.\n\nThus implementation is straightforward.\n\nImportant: The function must not mutate case, and must return a JSON-serializable dict. Must use only standard library.\n\nAlso note the output contract: required keys: decision, memory_append, next_attempt. memory_append can be null or object with reflection and signature. So we return exactly that.\n\nNow, write Python source.\n\nWe'll define solve(case) that takes the payload (which is the inner object). We'll extract attempts list and max_attempts. Compute logic, return dict.\n\nWrite as a function inside the implementation string.\n\nWe need to output a JSON object with key \"implementation\" and value the Python source as a JSON string. Escape properly.\n\nLet's write the code."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":1265,"completion_tokens":2481,"total_tokens":3746,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":1152},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":2084},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":1152,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":113},"system_fingerprint":"fp_8b330d02d0_prod0820_fp8_kvcache_20260402"}